This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-sanjo layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Dependencies
============

  URI: openembedded-core (poky)
  branch: scarthgap

Patches
=======

Please submit any patches against the meta-sanjo layer by opening a pull
request or issue on the GitHub repository.

Maintainer: Sanjo Sunny <sanjosunny2001@gmail.com>

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-sanjo layer to your build
 II. Layer contents
III. Misc


I. Adding the meta-sanjo layer to your build
=============================================

source poky/oe-init-build-env build
bitbake-layers add-layer meta-sanjo
bitbake core-image-minimal

II. Layer contents
===================

recipes-bmp280/
  bmp280 — BMP280 telemetry: IPC driver + Core 3 bare-metal writer + firstboot service.

recipes-bsp/
  bootfiles — board boot file customizations.

recipes-connectivity/
  wpa-supplicant — Wi-Fi configuration (wpa_supplicant.conf uses placeholder
  ssid/psk; override with real credentials via a local bbappend, do not
  commit real credentials to this layer).

recipes-core/
  images — core-image-minimal.bbappend customizing the base image.

recipes-example/
  example — starter recipe template created by bitbake-layers.

recipes-kernel/
  kernel-devsrc — kernel development source customizations.

recipes-telemetry/
  telemetry-daemon — telemetry daemon and web dashboard: reads the BMP280
  ring buffer, publishes system/board health over MQTT, and serves a
  lightweight HTTP dashboard.

III. Misc
=========

Target: Raspberry Pi, Yocto "scarthgap" release.
